Max Dillon / Electro, played by Jamie Foxx.

11
00:50:52,500 --> 00:50:58,500
Spider-Man: No Way Home is a 2021 American superhero film based on the Marvel Comics character Spider-Man,
co-produced by Columbia Pictures and Marvel Studios, and distributed by Sony Pictures Releasing.

12
00:55:30,000 --> 00:55:36,000
It is the sequel to Spider-Man: Homecoming (2017) and Spider-Man: Far From Home
(2019), and the 27th film in the Marvel Cinematic Universe (MCU).

13
01:00:07,500 --> 01:00:13,500
The film was directed by Jon Watts and written by
Chris McKenna and Erik Sommers.

14
01:04:45,000 --> 01:04:51,000
It stars Tom Holland as Peter Parker / Spider-Man alongside Zendaya, Benedict Cumberbatch, Jacob Batalon, Jon Favreau, Jamie
Foxx, Willem Dafoe, Alfred Molina, Benedict Wong, Tony Revolori, Marisa Tomei, Andrew Garfield, and Tobey Maguire.

15
01:09:22,500 --> 01:09:28,500
In the film, Peter asks Dr.

16
01:14:00,000 --> 01:14:06,000
Stephen Strange (Cumberbatch) to use magic to make his identity as Spider-Man a secret
again after it was revealed to the world at the end of Far From Home.

17
01:18:37,500 --> 01:18:43,500
When the spell goes wrong because of Peter's actions, the multiverse is broken open and
several visitors from alternate realities are brought into Peter's universe.

18
01:23:15,000 --> 01:23:21,000
A third MCU Spider-Man film was planned during the
production of Homecoming in 2017.

19
01:27:52,500 --> 01:27:58,500
Negotiations between Sony and Marvel Studios to alter their deal—in which they produce the Spider-Man films together—ended with Marvel
Studios leaving the project in August 2019, but a negative fan reaction led to a new deal between the companies a month later.

20
01:32:30,000 --> 01:32:36,000
Watts, McKenna, Sommers, and Holland were set to return, and filming took place
from October 2020 to March 2021 in New York City and Atlanta.

21
01:37:07,500 --> 01:37:13,500
No Way Home serves as a crossover between the MCU and the previous
Spider-Man films directed by Sam Raimi and Marc Webb.

22
01:41:45,000 --> 01:41:51,000
Several actors reprise their roles from those films, including
previous Spider-Man actors Maguire and Garfield.

23
01:46:22,500 --> 01:46:28,500
The pair's involvement was the subject of wide speculation and numerous leaks despite Sony,
Marvel, and the cast's efforts to conceal their involvement until the film's release.

24
01:51:00,000 --> 01:51:06,000
Spider-Man: No Way Home premiered at the Fox Village Theater in Westwood, Los Angeles, on December 13, 2021, and
was theatrically released in the United States on December 17, as part of Phase Four of the MCU.

25
01:55:37,500 --> 01:55:43,500
The film received positive reviews from critics and grossed $1.921 billion worldwide,
surpassing its predecessor as the highest-grossing film released by Sony Pictures.

26
02:00:15,000 --> 02:00:21,000
It became the highest-grossing film of 2021, the sixth-highest-grossing film at the time of its release, the highest-grossing
Spider-Man film, and set several other box office records, including those for films released during the COVID-19 pandemic.

27
02:04:52,500 --> 02:04:58,500
The film received a nomination for Best Visual Effects at the 94th
Academy Awards, among numerous other accolades.

28
02:09:30,000 --> 02:09:36,000
An extended version of the film, subtitled The More Fun Stuff
Version, had a global theatrical release in September 2022.

29
02:14:07,500 --> 02:14:13,500
An additional film trilogy with Holland is planned, beginning with Spider-Man:
Brand New Day, which is scheduled for release in July 2026.

30
02:18:45,000 --> 02:18:51,000
The film explores themes of new york city, hero,
showdown, magic, loss of loved one.

31
02:23:22,500 --> 02:23:28,500
The tone is thought_provoking.
